      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. one thing though... when people talk about \"security and stability\" or \"preservation\" as reasons to keep things, doesn't that kind of just sound like a way to justify keeping stolen goods? like, it feels a bit like saying 'we'll keep it because they can't take care of it' which was a big part of the original colonial argument. do u think those arguments still hold weight today or are they basically just excuses?",
